  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;premonition&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">The cracked mirror above the front door served as the innkeeper&apos;s reliable premonition of coming trouble, and she made a point of showing it to every single arriving guest.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">Counting down the days until the carnival finally arrived, Bea happily savored the premonition of cotton candy all week long.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">Marta had a premonition that the antique locket in the display case was hollow inside, and the jeweler confirmed it on the spot.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">Nothing about the morning was wrong, yet the shepherd&apos;s premonition pressed so hard that he penned the flock early — hours before the first tremor loosened the ridge.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A premonition is a feeling inside a person, not a thing on a wall — a cracked mirror treated as a sign to be read is an omen, and showing it to every guest only makes it more public and less felt.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A premonition arrives unbidden, about the unforeseen and usually the unwanted; Bea is counting down to a treat she already knows is scheduled, which is anticipation wearing the wrong name.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A premonition is about what is going to happen; Marta&apos;s flash concerns what the locket already is — hollow or not — which makes it a hunch about a present fact, not a warning of a coming one.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! A premonition is a strong, evidence-free feeling that something specific is about to happen — no sign, no reason, one particular fear, hours ahead of the tremor. Every requirement is met.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
